refentry.refsect1:
&reftitle.description;
mixedsnmp3_getnext stringhostname stringsecurity_name stringsecurity_level stringauth_protocol stringauth_passphrase stringprivacy_protocol stringprivacy_passphrase arraystringobject_id inttimeout-1 intretries-1
The snmp3_getnext function is used to read the value of the SNMP object that follows the specified object_id.

&reftitle.parameters;
hostname
The hostname of the SNMP agent (server). A port can be given after a colon, as in 127.0.0.1:1161. An IPv6 address must be enclosed in square brackets when a port is given, as in [::1]:1161.
security_name
&snmp.parameter.security-name;
security_level
&snmp.parameter.security-level;
auth_protocol
&snmp.parameter.auth-protocol;
auth_passphrase
&snmp.parameter.auth-passphrase;
privacy_protocol
&snmp.parameter.privacy-protocol;
privacy_passphrase
&snmp.parameter.privacy-passphrase;
object_id
The SNMP object id.
timeout
The number of microseconds to wait for an answer at each attempt. As every retry waits that long again, a call can last up to timeout multiplied by retries plus one. -1 uses the default of the Net-SNMP library, which is one second.
retries
The number of times to retry if timeouts occur. -1 uses the default of the Net-SNMP library, which is five retries.

&reftitle.changelog;





    &Version;
    &Description;





    8.5.0

     Now throws a ValueError when the hostname
     contains null bytes or is 128 bytes or longer, when the port is not
     between 0 and 65535, when the security name is empty or contains null
     bytes, when the timeout is lower than -1, or when the retries value is
     lower than -1 or greater than 2147483647.


   &snmp.changelog.privacy-protocol-aes;
   &snmp.changelog.auth-protocol-sha2;
